  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   We employ a continuous-domain function representation with periodic boundary conditions and minimize the maximum overlap integral. Unlike discrete grid optimization, this method uses smooth functional forms to exploit the structure of the problem. The centerpiece is a periodic basis expansion allowing adaptive resolution superseding traditional time-bound methods. We start with a known upper bound solution and seek to improve the C value by solving the optimization problem continuously. The central insight is that smooth, structured functions can achieve the minimum overlap. We combine gradient-driven optimization with confidence-controlled adaptive resolution to escape local optima.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   We represent the step function h(x) as:\n   h(x) = a0 + \u03a3_{k=1}^{m} [ak * cos(2\u03c0 k x) + bk * sin(2\u03c0 k x)]\n   with the constraint \u222b_{0}^{2} h(x) dx = 1 \u27f9 a0 = 0.5.\n   \n   \\subsubsection*{Objective} minimize C = max_{k=-\u221e}^{\u221e} \u222b_{0}^{2} h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n   \n   \\subsubsection*{Parameters} \u03b8 = (a1, b1, ..., am) \u2208 \u211d^{2m}, the unknown coefficients to optimize\n   \n   \\subsubsection*{Constraints}\n   - 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x\n   - \u222b h(x)dx = 1\n   \n   The optimization is performed with a penalty term that smoothens the max operation using a softmax-like approach. We employ satisfaction-of-measure projection to enforce interval constraints.\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   \\begin{enumerate}\n      \\item **Initialization:** Read parent solution (480 samples if provided), interpolate to function form\n      \\item **Parameter Extraction:** Compute function coefficients via orthogonal $L\u2082$ projection (Fourier series)\n      \\item **Phase 0 (Warm Start):** Use Avg-Default-LDAM-WF variant with $m=5$ frequencies\n      \\item **Phase 1 (Adaptive Growth):** Double solution resolution while maintaining coefficients\n      \\item **Phase 2 (Resolution Boost):** Stack higher-frequency variants from parent solution\n      \\item **Optimization Loop:** Continuous gradient optimization \n        - Compute \\(\\log\\)-sum-\\(exp\\) smoothed max\n        - Project solution to $[0,1]$ using layered clipping\n        \\item **Termination:** Monitor $\\Delta C < 10^{-6}$ or wall-clock stoppage\n   \\end{enumerate}\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n   \\begin{itemize}\n      \\item $m$ starts at 5 with $10^3$ iterations\n      \\item Doubles to 10, 20, 40 as resolution increases\n      \\item Classic 1D perturbation includes $\\sin(2\\pi x)$, $\\cos(2\\pi x)$\n      \\item Alternate representation uses complex exponential basis\n      \\item Select variation by RND=Uniform([0,1])\n      \\item Switch to integration-boosted formulation if $\\Delta f \\geq 0.01$\n   \\end{itemize}\n\n5. **Computation Budget and Robustness**\n   \\begin{itemize}\n      \\item Total FLOPs: $6 \\times 480^3 = 6.6 \\times 10^9$ (avoided by adaptive projection)\n      \\item Timers: Local 10-sec checks, global 1300s budget\n      \\item Error handling: Retry with larger $m$ if overflow occurs\n      \\item Fall back: Lin-Bary projection if projection attempts >3 fail\n      \\item Memory: 2\u00d7 current array storage at each resolution level\n      \\item Performance: Parallelized integration across 8 lags\n   \\end{itemize}\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n   \\begin{itemize}\n      \\item Redundant checks: Curve clipping at $\\epsilon=1e-6$\n      \\item Resampling certainty: Evaluate at 1000 random lags\n      \\item Backup validation: Re-discretize with parent's resolution to $\\delta=1e-6$ tolerance\n      \\item Final output: Roundtrip consistency (fourier/interpolated forms)\n      \\item Success threshold: $C < 0.3808$\n      \\item Failure protocol: Lowpass fallback and termination\n      \\item Metrics: Wall time tracking, C update frequency logging\n   \\end{itemize}",
